WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
A lot of people don't talk about this,

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:04.640
but entrepreneurship will mess with your

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.120
life in ways that you're not even

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.760
prepared for. And if you're not ready

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.640
for these seven truths, then you

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:11.320
probably shouldn't even start. So, I

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.840
built multiple seven and eight-figure

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.080
businesses, and I'm going to tell you

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.000
the things that I wish somebody told me

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.480
before I started on the journey. And if

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.200
at any point throughout the video you

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.280
get any value, do me a huge favor.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.040
Please go ahead and like it. It helps me

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.640
out a ton, and will get this video in

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.400
front of more people who need to see it.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.240
So, let's get into it with truth number

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.960
one. And that is that you will feel

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.520
alone even when you're winning. And most

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.480
people don't expect that. You know, you

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.560
hit a milestone, you cross a revenue

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.120
threshold that you used to dream about,

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.080
and instead of feeling the way that you

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.920
thought you would, you feel nothing.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.000
Sometimes even worse than nothing. And

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.680
the reason why is because you can't talk

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.480
to anybody about it. You can't talk to

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.880
your employees the way that you used to

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.200
talk to coworkers because your employees

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.680
look to you for answers now. They watch

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.440
how you react. You're the guy. So, you

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.600
can't really show the doubt that you

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.680
have. You can't vent to anybody because

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.480
you're the guy at the very top. And that

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.280
means that you have to carry a lot of

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.080
the weight alone. Then there's your old

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.160
friends, the ones you grew up with, went

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.920
to school with, hung out with before any

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.600
of this. You love them, but they don't

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.200
understand your world anymore. They

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.960
don't get why you're stressed when

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.080
you're making all that money. They don't

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.840
understand what a $200,000 payroll week

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.960
feels like. They don't understand why

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.040
you can't just relax on the weekends or

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.840
hang out on a random Sunday. So, you end

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.160
up outgrowing people. Not because you're

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.160
better than them, but because you're

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.200
living a completely different reality

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.000
than them. I oversee hundreds of people

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.760
across my different organizations, and

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.520
I'll be the first to tell you that the

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.360
loneliness doesn't go away with scale.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.160
The bigger you build, the fewer people

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.920
can actually relate to what you're

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.840
carrying. And the tough part is that

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.840
there's nobody above you to hand it to.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.480
There is no safety net. So, you just

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.360
carry it every day. And if you're not

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:53.400
careful, the weight becomes a bit

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.280
numbing. You stop feeling the wins. You

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:57.240
stop really feeling much of anything. It

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.960
reminds me of what Hormozi said in his

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.800
episode with Tony Robbins,

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.320
Happiness. And this is why a lot of

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.000
entrepreneurs self-destruct at this

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.840
stage. Not because the business is

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.560
failing, but because they never learned

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.000
how to cope with this version of

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.959
success, or they have a constant need to

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.600
achieve. So, they find ways to deal with

00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:16.280
that feeling, and it could be drinking,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.680
toxic behaviors, anything to compensate

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:20.600
for an emptiness underneath it all. But,

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.560
there is a bright side. The solution is

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:24.320
to find your people. And it could be

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.320
other entrepreneurs that can relate to

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.200
you, or that you can trust, or a mentor,

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.800
or a life coach, somebody who's been

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.080
where you're going. It could even be

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.760
your spouse who can be your soundboard.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.600
You don't need everybody to understand

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.640
your world. You just need a couple of

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:39.640
people that actually get it, and that

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:41.680
will change everything. So, truth number

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.800
two is that money will not fix your

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.120
problems, okay? Now, this might seem

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.640
hard to believe, and I didn't believe it

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.520
either. But, here's what happens when

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.640
the money comes in. As your revenue

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.080
grows, so does everything else. Your

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.040
payroll, your overhead, your liability,

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.360
everything scales with you. So, a

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.840
mistake that used to cost you five grand

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.480
now costs you 50 grand. You trade I

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.680
can't pay my bills stress for a

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.280
different type of stress. Things like I

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.720
have a hundred people depending on me,

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.320
or if this deal falls apart, I will

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.280
still need to come up with the money for

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.959
payroll. And that is probably why so

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:15.959
many entrepreneurs struggle mentally,

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:18.200
not because they're failing, but because

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:20.920
nobody prepared them for this side of

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:23.160
it. And 87% of them deal with at least

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.400
one mental health issue. Half struggle

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:27.440
with anxiety, and a third they burn out

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.200
completely. So, money fixes your old

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.480
problems, but for every problem it

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.160
solves, it creates two more problems.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.200
You wanted revenue, but now you need

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:37.040
systems to manage it. You wanted a team,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.959
but now you need to lead the team. You

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.400
wanted to scale, and now you have to

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:44.160
sustain the scale. So, the finish line

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:46.200
doesn't exist. It just moves, and now

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.519
you have a new goal. So, truth number

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.000
three is that nobody actually knows what

00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:51.519
they're doing. So, let me destroy an

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.640
illusion for you. That eight-figure

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:55.360
operator that you follow on IG, they're

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.000
figuring it out in real time. The

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.800
founder who just raised a series B, they

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.280
have no idea what next quarter looks

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:04.080
like. Me, I'm constantly operating in

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:06.040
uncertainty. I've built multiple

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.280
companies. I've done deals most people

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.480
can only dream about, and I still

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:12.440
encounter situations every single day of

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.320
my life where I have to make a call that

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.400
I've never made before with incomplete

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.480
information, knowing that I could be

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.680
totally wrong. Everybody at the top is

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.720
improvising, okay? The confident ones

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:25.080
just stopped waiting for certainty

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.600
before they moved. This should liberate

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.560
you. You're not behind because you don't

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.360
have all the answers. Nobody does. The

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.840
question is whether you're willing to

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.440
move anyway. Okay, so truth number four

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.360
is speed beats intelligence every single

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.720
time.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.520
And I want to be direct about this one

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:41.760
because I've seen it actually destroy a

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.800
lot of really talented people. I have

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:45.680
competed against people who are smarter

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.640
than me, better connected than me, with

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.520
more resources than me, and I beat them

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.880
repeatedly. And you want to know why?

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.320
Because while everybody else was

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.360
analyzing, making a pros and a cons, I

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:57.200
was executing. In real estate, I've won

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.760
deals that I had no business winning.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.600
Deals where the other buyer had more

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:03.640
capital, more experience, and more

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:05.440
leverage because I moved in 24 hours and

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:07.360
they moved in a week. Sellers don't want

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:09.400
the best offer in 2 weeks from now. They

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:12.160
want a real offer today. So,

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:13.800
overthinking is the most expensive habit

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.520
that an entrepreneur can have, okay? It

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:19.840
feels productive, it feels responsible,

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:21.520
but it is not. The market rewards speed,

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.480
and your competition is not sitting

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.480
around for you to get comfortable. So,

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.360
every day that you spend getting ready

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:29.560
is a day that somebody else is in the

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.600
market building experience that you

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:33.919
don't have yet. Done is better than

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.520
perfect, and imperfect action beats

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:38.320
perfect inaction every single time.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:40.720
Truth number five is that your first

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:42.520
business might not or probably won't be

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.280
your biggest one. This is the one that

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:46.000
most people in the early stages need to

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.200
hear. So, if that's you, pay attention.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.960
Your first business is school. It's

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:52.280
where you learn how to run a business,

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:55.080
how to hire people, how to sell, how to

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.360
manage cash flow, read a P&L, and how to

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.480
recover from mistakes. I didn't start in

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.520
pest control. I started in real estate.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:03.200
I started wholesaling, flipping, and

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.840
then I became an agent, grinding through

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:07.920
deals one by one. And that taught me

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.800
operations. It taught me systems, how to

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.600
manage people, how to hire people. And

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:13.920
when I launched Nectar Pest Control, I

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.720
brought all of that with me. Most

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.880
successful entrepreneurs that you know,

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.960
they've pivoted at one point or another.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:21.680
They started somewhere, they iterated,

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.640
they got smarter, and they built

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.919
something bigger off the back of what

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.600
they learned. The path is very rarely

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:29.800
linear in a straight line, right? The

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.919
problem is that people quit after the

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:34.000
first business doesn't blow up. They

00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:35.640
treat the first attempt as the verdict

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.520
instead of the training. And your first

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:39.480
business is not your destiny. It is your

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:41.560
education. Stay in it long enough to

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:43.240
learn the lesson, then take that lesson

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.200
and build something bigger with it.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:46.760
Truth number six, you will work more

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.240
than you've ever worked in your entire

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.760
life. And I'm going to say something

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:51.800
that's going to upset a lot of people

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:54.160
selling you the dream online. Escape the

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:56.720
9-to-5 is the biggest lie in

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:58.760
entrepreneurship. Yeah, eventually, with

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:00.320
the right systems and the right team,

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:02.560
you can build a business that doesn't

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:04.480
require your constant presence. You

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.240
don't trade a 9-to-5 for freedom. You

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.480
trade it for 24/7. Not always physically

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:11.560
in the office, but mentally, right? Your

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.919
business lives in your head all the

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.160
time. A lot of people can't relate to

00:07:12.919 --> 00:07:15.919
this. You're thinking about it at

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.320
dinner. You wake up at 3:00 a.m. with a

00:07:15.919 --> 00:07:19.160
problem you forgot to solve. You're

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:21.200
taking notes on your nightstand. A deal

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.840
goes sideways on a Saturday, and you're

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:24.480
by the pool, and you're handling it from

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.280
your phone. You're on your way to a

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:28.040
family function, you're in the car. The

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:30.200
mental load of entrepreneurship is

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.720
something that nobody prepares you for.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:35.080
It isn't just hours, it's the weight of

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.120
carrying the entire organization, the

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:39.760
decisions, the people, the payroll, the

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:41.520
uncertainty, with nobody above you to

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.360
hand it to. And I'm not saying this to

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.040
scare you. I'm saying it because if you

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.520
go into this expecting to work less and

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:49.800
you're not willing to go through the

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:52.120
hard years, you'll quit right before it

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:54.120
gets good. The freedom is real, but you

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:55.960
earn it. There are no shortcuts through

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.200
this part. And finally, truth number

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:00.640
seven, most people don't actually want

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:02.320
success, they want the idea of it. And

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:03.880
this is the hardest truth and I say it

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:06.480
without judgment because I've seen it in

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:08.160
myself, too. It's easy to want success

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:10.400
when you're imagining the result, the

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:12.720
lifestyle, the autonomy, the financial

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:15.680
security. The part that feels good to

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:17.480
want. What's hard is to want the path

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.520
that it actually takes to achieve that.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:21.640
The rejection, the failed deals, the

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.480
employees who quit on you or stole from

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:25.440
you, the months where your business is

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.280
bleeding cash and you're not sure if

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.120
you're going to make it. The

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:29.720
relationships that take a hit, the

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.880
sacrifices that don't feel like

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:34.360
sacrifices in motivational content that

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:36.159
you watch, but feel very real at 11:00

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:38.080
p.m. when you're exhausted,

00:08:36.159 --> 00:08:40.159
second-guessing every decision that

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.880
you've made. Most people, they hit that

00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:44.039
and they stop. And here's what they tell

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.880
themselves, "I tried, it didn't work,

00:08:44.039 --> 00:08:47.040
and entrepreneurship is just not for

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.720
me." But that isn't really what

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:51.440
happened. What happened is that they

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:54.480
found out what it actually cost and they

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:56.320
decided that the cost was simply not

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:58.640
worth it to them, which is a completely

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.320
valid choice. Not everybody should be an

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.720
entrepreneur, and I mean that from the

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.320
bottom of my heart. But if you're

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:05.000
watching this, especially if you're

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:07.480
still watching this, you need to ask

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:10.440
yourself an honest question. Do you want

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:12.240
the success or do you want the idea of

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.760
success? Because one of those will get

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:15.400
you through the hard years and one of

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.880
them won't. The people who make it

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.560
aren't the most talented in the world.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:20.680
They're the ones who are still there

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:22.640
when everybody left. So much of

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:24.839
entrepreneurship is simply just

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.120
outlasting everybody. My name is Austin

00:09:24.839 --> 00:09:27.800
Zeeback and it would mean the world to

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.080
me if you would subscribe to my channel

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.680
and like the video. It would help this

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:32.400
channel out a ton and go check out these

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:33.440
two videos right here. I think they

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:36.839
would help you and I look forward to

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:36.839
seeing you in a future video.

